  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2020-07-17T01:00:09.129Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Having an Animation present within an Animator that affects the root scale causes the avatar's root scale to be incorrect when using it. \nThis happens even if the state containing the Animation isn't active or the weight of the layer is 0. It also doesn't matter what the scale is set to within the Animation (as long as it isn't the same as it was originally).\nCurrently the only workaround for this is to have a separate Animation constantly playing that sets the scale correctly until it needs to be changed.\nThis can be replicated using a custom Action layer that has a state containing an Animation that modifies the root scale and testing the avatar in game. (The Action layer's weight does not need to be set to 1).\nVideo: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZlMf-uyt2uI",
